# Build output.
#
# `/target` alone is not enough. `apps/desktop/src-tauri` is its own cargo
# workspace -- it has to be, because Tauri pins a different dependency graph than
# the engine and sharing a lockfile between them produces two irreconcilable
# resolution attempts -- so it gets its own target directory too. `/target`
# matches exactly one directory at the root and silently misses it.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Local queue files, if anyone runs the CLI from a checkout. These contain the
# URLs the user downloaded; they are not ours to publish even accidentally.
ifami-queue.json
*.part

# Nothing in this project reads an environment variable, and the intention is to
# keep it that way. These are here so that a future `.env` is a decision rather
# than an accident, and so gitleaks has less to do.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build and test output that is not cargo's.
coverage/
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
node_modules/
apps/desktop/dist/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej

# Merge and patch leftovers. Refusing to be silently ignored is the point: a
# `.orig` file in a commit is a merge that went wrong, and it should be visible.
*.patch
*.diff